ARC country.\nB. For non-Indian candidates from other SAARC countries, the admission to various Bachelors/Masters/PhD programmes will also be made on the basis of their scores obtained in their qualifying examination. For this purpose, a list of various schools/colleges/universities/institutions is being considered and approved by the University whose students\nwill be considered for admission to SAU without going through the SAU Entrance Test.\nc) For Non-SAARC candidates\nFor non-SAARC candidates, the admission to various Bachelors/Masters/PhD programmes will be made on the basis of their scores obtained in their qualifying examination.\nNote:\nCandidates\napplying\nthrough\nthe\nDirect\nMode\nmust\npay\nthe\nApplication/Registration Fee for each programme separately. However, in the Entrance Mode, candidates applying for programmes that share the same entrance test are required to pay the fee for one programme only.").
